        "original_id": "1a0ab63b-6b8f-5c26-862f-dfa3ebd24f97",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patrick McEnroe, Billie Jean King, Larry King, Boris Becker, Guy Forget, Jim Grabb\n- Events: 1990 Newsweek Champions Cup – Doubles\n- Roles: professional tennis player, Davis Cup captain, attorney, real estate broker, promoter, World Team Tennis founder\n- Organizations: United States Davis Cup team, World Team Tennis\n\nFacts:\n- Billie Jean King was born as Billie Jean Moffitt on November 22, 1943, and she is an American former World No. 1 professional tennis player.\n- Larry King was born on January 30, 1945, and he is an American attorney, real estate broker, promoter, one of the founders of World Team Tennis, and the former husband of Billie Jean King.\n- Patrick John McEnroe was born on July 1, 1966, and he is a former professional tennis player and former captain of the United States Davis Cup team.\n- In the 1990 Newsweek Champions Cup – Doubles final, Boris Becker and Guy Forget defeated Jim Grabb and Patrick McEnroe 4–6, 6–4, 6–3 to win the title.",
